[node name="GeoReference" type="Node" parent="." unique_id=1000000073]
script = null
meta = """
CAPE TOWN CBD BLOCKOUT - GEOGRAPHIC REFERENCE DOCUMENTATION

REAL-WORLD COORDINATE SYSTEM:
- Origin (0,0,0) in this scene corresponds to the intersection of Long Street and Strand Street
- X axis: East-West (positive = East, towards Wale Street)
- Z axis: North-South (positive = South, away from Table Mountain / towards Buitengracht)
- Y axis: Height above street level (meters)

REAL GEOGRAPHIC COORDINATES (WGS84):
- Long Street & Strand Street intersection: -33.9185, 18.4195
- Long Street & Buitengracht Street intersection: -33.9205, 18.4195
- Wale Street & Strand Street intersection: -33.9185, 18.4215
- Wale Street & Buitengracht Street intersection: -33.9205, 18.4215
- Castle of Good Hope center: -33.9265, 18.4285
- Cape Town City Hall: -33.9245, 18.4245
- Grand Parade center: -33.9245, 18.4245
- Greenmarket Square: -33.9205, 18.4185
- Table Mountain peak: -33.9628, 18.4098

SCENE SCALE:
- 1 Godot unit = 1 meter
- Block dimensions based on typical Cape Town CBD city blocks (~80-100m per side)
- Road widths: ~20m (Strand St, Buitengracht St) / ~20m (Long St, Wale St, Bree St, Hout St)
- Pavement widths: ~4m each side
- Building heights: 8-28m (2-8 stories typical for CBD)

STREETS INCLUDED (verified from OpenStreetMap / City of Cape Town GIS):
1. Strand Street (N1 foreshore route) - East/West, northern boundary
2. Buitengracht Street - East/West, one block south of Strand
3. Plein Street - East/West, center of block
4. Spin Street - East/West, between Buitengracht and Strand
5. Long Street - North/South, western commercial corridor
6. Bree Street - North/South, one block west of Long
7. Hout Street - North/South, between Bree and Long
8. Wale Street - North/South, one block east of Long (leads to Bo-Kaap)

LANDMARK SILHOUETTES (approximate positions, simplified massing):
- Castle of Good Hope: Pentagonal fort, east of CBD (X=+80, Z=+40)
- Cape Town City Hall: Edwardian building, north of Castle (X=-80, Z=+40)
- Grand Parade: Large public square between City Hall and Castle (X=-40, Z=+40)
- Greenmarket Square: Historic market square, west of Long St (X=-40, Z=-60)
- Table Mountain: Distant backdrop, south of city (Z=-1000, Y=500+)

